    "report": "The message notice now carries `listingId`, and the change is committed as `a26b614` on `main`. I did not push. Typecheck, conventions check, lint, format and the full unit suite (155 suites, 1,049 tests) pass, and the full e2e run passes after updating two assertions.\n\n**What changed, end to end:**\n- **Messaging** records `listingId` on `MessageSentEvent` in both places a message is written (conversation start and later messages). `MessageSentHandler` passes it on.\n- **Shared kernel** `MessageSentPayload` gains `listingId`. This file is under `src/SharedKernel`, which the CLAUDE.md feature-mode note calls out. The change is the payload field the contract needs, so I made it and am flagging it here.\n- **Notifications** carries it through `SentMessage` → `MessageNoticeOwing` → `MessageNoticeBody`, and stores it in the existing `notices.listing_id` column. No migration is needed.\n- **Who is told, how often, and delivery** are unchanged. The other notice kinds are untouched.\n\n**Choices and open points:**\n- **Pending notices from before the deploy** have no stored listing id. When they are resent they will go out with `\"listingId\": null`. I did not backfill them, because that would mean a lookup in Messaging. If the notification service needs the id on those, a backfill is a separate decision.\n- **Commit branch:** you asked for the commit on the current branch, which is `main`. I committed there as instructed rather than creating a branch.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected bodies in three unit specs and in two e2e specs (`message-notices.e2e.spec.ts`, `messageClock.routes.e2e.spec.ts`) to include `listingId`.\n- **Not run:** I did not use the `clean-ddd knowledge` command, and I did not regenerate any inventory, since no command, route or event name changed.",
